From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valix <djvalic.wc@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:01:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: ingenic: cgu: Start a stopped divider on enable

A CGU divider with a stop bit gives no clock while that bit is set, and
the driver clears it only in set_rate(). A clock that is enabled but
never given a new rate keeps the stop bit as it was found, so if
whatever ran before Linux left the divider stopped, the clock stays off
although the clock framework counts it as enabled.

On the Flashforge AD5X (X2600) the PWM divider (PWMCDR) reads
0x2800000f: its stop bit is set. The X2600 PWM driver enables its clock
and never sets its rate, so the PWM channels get no clock and the
speaker on PC12 stays silent. Ingenic's own clock driver clears the
stop bit when it enables a divider.

Clear the stop bit on enable too, with the change enable bit and the
busy wait as set_rate() does, before the gate is opened (the order of
Ingenic's driver, where the gate is the divider's child). A divider
that is not stopped is not written.
---
 drivers/clk/ingenic/cgu.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/ingenic/cgu.c b/drivers/clk/ingenic/cgu.c
index 0605a969a..1def63fc4 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/ingenic/cgu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/ingenic/cgu.c
@@ -651,6 +651,30 @@ static int ingenic_clk_enable(struct clk_hw *hw)
 	const struct ingenic_cgu_clk_info *clk_info = to_clk_info(ingenic_clk);
 	struct ingenic_cgu *cgu = ingenic_clk->cgu;
 	unsigned long flags;
+	int ret = 0;
+	u32 reg;
+
+	if ((clk_info->type & CGU_CLK_DIV) && clk_info->div.stop_bit != -1) {
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&cgu->lock, flags);
+		reg = readl(cgu->base + clk_info->div.reg);
+
+		/* start a stopped divider, as set_rate() does */
+		if (reg & BIT(clk_info->div.stop_bit)) {
+			reg &= ~BIT(clk_info->div.stop_bit);
+
+			if (clk_info->div.ce_bit != -1)
+				reg |= BIT(clk_info->div.ce_bit);
+
+			writel(reg, cgu->base + clk_info->div.reg);
+
+			if (clk_info->div.busy_bit != -1)
+				ret = ingenic_clk_check_stable(cgu, clk_info);
+		}
+
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&cgu->lock, flags);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}

 	if (clk_info->type & CGU_CLK_GATE) {
 		/* ungate the clock */
--
